On Fri, 2026-11-27 at 11:08 -0800, Andrew Morton wrote:
> On Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:46:58 +0000 "Lorenzo Stoakes (ARM)"
> <ljs@kernel.org> wrote:
>=20
> > I've got the distinct impression my views are not welcome on this
> > topic,
> > rather had that feeling from the start
>=20
> I agree with everything Lorenzo has written!
>=20
>=20
> I dunno Sasha, everything here seems rather .... wordy.
>=20
> Has anyone tried this:
>=20
> - find some tens of *good* changelogs
>=20
> - get it to crunch on those in order to
> =C2=A0 generate how-to-write-changelogs.md
>=20
> - argue with it for an hour, as always
>=20
> - add how-to-write-changelogs.md to Linux

I pointed it at a few decades of my commit messages and lkml posts, and
a few other things I'd written, and told it to come up with a 'dwmw2-
voice' skill.

I feel *seen*, and it only kind of works. I still frequently have to
remind it of what I tell my children: never use words, where silence
will suffice.

